house first, before you build the main house. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:26.880 --> 00:56:33.200
if you use paper to build a dummy house first,&nbsp;
before building the main house, it's going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:33.200 --> 00:56:39.280
a lot easier when the owner of the house comes&nbsp;
to make a correction or comes to make a change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:39.280 --> 00:56:45.040
Since it's a paper, you don't have much to lose,&nbsp;
all you have to do is just tear it and put it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:45.040 --> 00:56:51.920
back in seconds. But if you go ahead to build the&nbsp;
main house first, and the owner of the house comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:51.920 --> 00:56:58.000
and says, Okay, I don't want this design here, I&nbsp;
don't want that there, it means that you'd have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:58.000 --> 00:57:04.720
break down that part of the house and rebuild that&nbsp;
part of the house with all of the resources that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:04.720 --> 00:57:10.720
you have put into building that part of the house.&nbsp;
